          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em Chern-Simons circle 7-bundle
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle 7-bundle with connection
            classified by the cocycle in degree-8
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            that is canonically associated to a
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+group"} string group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+2-bundle"} connection
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+class"} characteristic class
            called the second fractional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin+class"} Pontryagin class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 6
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 2
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mi String
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℬ
                    %mn 8
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{1}{6}p_2 : \mathcal{B}String \to \mathcal{B}^8 \mathbb{Z}
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+group"} string group
            has a smooth lift to the
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/edit/Lie+infinity-groupoid#SmoothSecondPontryagin"} smooth second fractional Pontryagin class
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 6
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi p
                    %mn 2
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi String
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 7
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\frac{1}{6} \mathbf{p}_2 : \mathbf{B}String \to \mathbf{B}^7 U(1)
          %p
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} :=
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9ELieGrpd"} ∞LieGrpd
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+groupoid"} ∞-Lie groupoid
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+Lie+2-group"} string Lie 2-group
            to that of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Lie+infinity-groupoid#BnU1"} circle Lie 7-group
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Lie+infinity-groupoid#IntegrationOfCocycles"} Lie integration
            of the degree 7
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra+cocycle"} ∞-Lie algebra cocycle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mn 7
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝔰𝔱𝔯𝔦𝔫𝔤
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mn 6
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_7 : \mathfrak{string} \to b^6 \mathbb{R}
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+Lie+2-algebra"} string Lie 2-algebra
            which classified the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fivebrane+Lie+6-algebra"} fivebrane Lie 6-algebra
          %p
            Therefore, by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Weil+theory"} ∞-Chern-Weil theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+an+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} ∞-bundles with connection
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 6
                  %mover
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi String
                    %mi conn
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 7
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\frac{1}{6}\hat \mathbf{p} : \mathbf{B}String_{conn} \to
                  \\mathbf{B}^7 U(1)_{conn}
          %p
            hence on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 6
                  %mover
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mi conn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi String
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mi diff
                    %mn 8
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\frac{1}{6} \hat \mathbf{p} : \mathbf{H}_{conn}(X,\mathbf{B}String)
                  \\to \mathbf{H}_{diff}^8(X)
          %p
            a map from
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+Lie+2-group"} string Lie 2-group
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+2-bundle"} connection
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle 7-bundles with connection
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (P,\nabla)
            a String-principal 2-bundle, we call the image
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 6
                  %mover
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mi diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 7
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{1}{6}\hat\mathbf{p}(\nabla) \in \mathbf{H}_{diff}(X,\mathbf{B}^7 U(1))
            its
            = succeed "." do
              %strong Chern-Simons circle 7-bundle with connection
          %p
            This is a differential refinement of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} obstruction
            to lifting
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            to a
            = succeed "-bundle." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fivebrane+Lie+6-group"} fivebrane Lie 6-group
          %p
            By construction, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            8-form of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat \mathbf{c}(\nabla)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature+characteristic+form"} curvature characteristic form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle F_\nabla \wedge F_\nabla \wedge F_\nabla \wedge F_\nabla\rangle
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
            and accordingly the 7-form connection on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat \mathbf{c}(\nabla)
            is locally a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+form"} Chern-Simons form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CS
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CS(\nabla)
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∇
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
          %p
            Therefore the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+parallel+transport"} higher parallel transport
            induced by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 6
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{1}{6}\hat \mathbf{p}_2(\nabla)
            over 7-dimensional volumes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo :
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : \Sigma \to X
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            of degree-7
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Simons+theory"} ∞-Chern-Simons theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+circle+3-bundle"} Chern-Simons circle 3-bundle
            arises from Spin-principal bundles.
          %h2#construction Construction
          %p
            Using the discussion at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Weil+theory"} ∞-Chern-Weil theory
            and in direct analogy to the construction of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+circle+3-bundle"} Chern-Simons circle 3-bundle
            we can model the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mi conn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi String
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mi conn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 7
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{H}_{conn}(X, \mathbf{B}String)
                  \\to
                  \\mathbf{H}_{conn}(X, \mathbf{B}^7 U(1))
          %p
            by postcomposition with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-anafunctor"} ∞-anafunctor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi exp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi 𝔰𝔱𝔯𝔦𝔫𝔤
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi conn
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi exp
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi μ
                                %mn 7
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mi conn
                        %mtd
